# Chronicle Plan execution adapter

Apply this rule only while the shared `execute-todo` or `execute-plan` Skill is active.

## Plans and branches

- Plans live under `.cursor/plans/*.plan.md`.
- Prefer branch names in the form `<type>/p<N.N>-<short-task-name>` unless the active plan defines a more specific convention.
- Execute TODOs serially in the primary worktree by default.
- Before each TODO, the main Agent fetches remote state, switches to `main`, fast-forwards with `git pull --ff-only origin main`, then creates or switches to the current TODO branch.
- The Worker implements and verifies on that already prepared branch. It must not switch branches or perform Git delivery.
- Do not begin the next TODO until the current TODO is accepted, merged, local `main` is synchronized, and the finished branch is deleted.
- Use an additional worktree only when the user explicitly requests parallel execution.

## Verification

Choose checks by changed scope:

- Frontend: `npm test`, `npm run lint`, and `npm run build` as required by the TODO.
- Python pipeline: run the relevant tests under `scripts/tests/` with `python -m pytest`.
- Locale structure changes: run `npx vitest run frontend/src/lib/locales/locales.schema.spec.ts` from the repository root.
- Do not run expensive full data rebuilds unless the TODO or user explicitly requires them.

## Completion artifacts

- After main-Agent technical acceptance and any required human approval, the main Agent first updates the canonical Plan TODO status to `complete`, then writes the final report under `docs/reports/` on the same TODO branch.
- The main Agent reviews the implementation, Plan status, and report as one TODO-owned diff before finalization.
- This repository uses `finish_todo.sh` to commit all remaining accepted TODO changes, push, create a PR, merge, synchronize `main`, and delete the task branch.
- On Windows, invoke it through Git Bash with `FINISH_TODO_MESSAGE` as documented by the script.
- Never run `finish_todo.sh` before required technical/human acceptance or without explicit authorization to commit, push, create a PR, and merge. A matching `execute-todo` or `execute-plan` command supplies that standard Git delivery authorization.
- After the script completes, independently verify that the PR is merged, the merged commit is reachable from local `main`, the primary worktree is on synchronized `main`, and the TODO branch is deleted before starting another TODO.

## PR checks and merge

- Determine hard merge gates from actual GitHub branch protection/rulesets and from checks explicitly required by the active TODO or user. Do not infer a hard gate from a failed status alone.
- `Cloudflare Pages` / CFP is an advisory preview check by default in this repository. Its failure must be reported but must not block an accepted and authorized merge when GitHub permits the merge.
- If GitHub rejects the merge because a required check or review is actually configured, stop and report that exact hard gate. Never bypass a real protection rule.
